cpp-pinyin provides CMake targets:

  find_package(cpp-pinyin2 CONFIG REQUIRED)
  target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE cpp-pinyin2::cpp-pinyin2)

To use the library, you need to copy the dictionary files to the binary directory.

  add_custom_command(TARGET main POST_BUILD
      COMMAND "${CMAKE_COMMAND}" -E copy_directory
        "${CPP_PINYIN2_DICT_DIR}"
        "$<TARGET_FILE_DIR:main>/dict"
  )

cpp-pinyin provides pkg-config modules:

  # A lightweight Chinese/Cantonese to Pinyin library.
  cpp-pinyin2
